  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Physical Description
    
    A tapered column of whale-bone, seven feet high, darkened by pressure and age to the color of frozen blood. Deep-sea coral winds around its base in spirals whose purpose — decorative or ritual — no living orca can confirm. The surface bears carved kill-counts: notches, tooth-marks, and sigils in no script recognized by any tradition of the Berg. Not orca pressure-song. Not Aurora celestial notation. Not Nightshelf tunnel-chant marks. The carvings are reported to shift when not observed directly. Near the apex, three symbols of the dead god worshipped by the orca were gouged out with such violence that the white bone beneath is exposed. This defacement appears to predate the shaping of the Berg itself.
    
    The designation "M7-6HH39N" belongs to a classification system that predates orca memory. The letters and numbers correspond to no living script.
    
    ## Origins
    
    All three creation traditions — Wake-Singer, Aurora liturgical, and Nightshelf fire-keeper — acknowledge the Obelisk's presence at the Berg's founding, and none claim authorship. The orca account holds it was found already embedded inside the dead god's body, "the way flesh closes over a splinter, incorporating what it cannot expel." The chronicle *The Holding of the Berg* records that the three primordial shapers — Grandmother Deep, the orca theology's guiding intelligence; Shadow-Broker Nyla, then of the Nightshelf; and High-Beak Auditor Selka of the Aurora — each tested the artifact with their sovereign magic and failed. Grandmother Deep's pressure-sight found it opaque. Nyla's fire-knowledge found it temperatureless. Selka's aurora-light pooled at its base and went dark.
    
    The deep ice, which records everything else, holds no memory of this object. I have checked. The relevant strata contain a gap in the precise shape of a pillar — not absence but erasure, or something that was never there to record. In thirty-one years of reading the Foundation Depths, I have encountered nothing comparable.
    
    ## Discovery and Custody
    
    The Obelisk was uncovered at the Corpse Current, an underwater convergence sacred to the Wake-Singers where the Berg's memory reportedly leaks into the present. The unnamed traveler who found it claimed it spoke to her in pressure-dreams. She surrendered it to the Wake-Singers, the orca shamanic cult that conducts blood-rituals to wake their dead god. Three months later she drowned herself in the Nightshelf's thermal pools, her lungs full of scalding water and what was described as coral spawn.
    
    The artifact corrupted three Fire Keeper smiths before the Wake-Singers assumed formal custody during the Faction Wars. Every guardian since has reported the same pressure-dreams — not visions of triumph but of the dead god's jaws closing on the dreamer. The ice around the artifact never fully freezes. Aurora-light refuses the space surrounding it.
    
    ## Containment and the Abyss Collapse Tide
    
    The Obelisk was transferred into the Nightshelf tunnels and moved progressively deeper. When Augur ☽'Silvsiaelrous~ the Resolute, a powerful augur of the ☽'shadow Covens' Order, attempted to bury it permanently, the resulting catastrophe — the Abyss Collapse Tide — consumed the surrounding galleries and killed ☽'Silvsiaelrous~ herself. The Obelisk survived. Explorers dispatched months later found it *higher* than where it had been placed. Rising.
    
    ☽'Saetacaeia-Viamana~, a Nightshelf mystic of the Communion who had mastered three forbidden magics, eventually descended to the containment chamber and performed the ☽'glacial Crystalline~ Spiral in reverse against the Obelisk's surface — surrendering her accumulated knowledge rather than wielding it. The artifact sank several inches. Its coral cracked and darkened. The weeping ice began to freeze. It is sealed by knowledge freely given rather than destroyed by force, though the Wake-Singers have not confirmed it has stopped rising entirely.
    
    ## Use at Terrace Momiou
    
    Despite its containment, the Obelisk was transported to Terrace Momiou by a Midnight Claws squad — the Nightshelf covert operations faction — who referred to it as "the Bastard." It served as the focal point for the Grulkzul Omega Strike, channeling deep-pressure through its whale-bone core while three incompatible magical sources were fused through its surface. The casting cracked the Obelisk down its full length and reduced the basal coral to lifeless char.
    
    A single pale tendril of new growth has since appeared at the base.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
  annotation "note_1771579366910_0", anchor: "Shadow-Broker Nyla, then of the Nightshelf", text: "Nyla is alive. Nyla confessed to murder before the Aurora Stack council within living memory. Placing her at the Berg's founding alongside a primordial orca shaper is not anachronism — it is temporal vertigo. The chronicle names her as though she were there. She was not there. No title 'Shadow-Broker' appears in any founding-era record I have accessed, and the lineage itself is compromised: Nyla's predecessor held the role from Aurora Stack, not the Nightshelf, a fact the official histories were quietly amended to obscure. Either 'The Holding of the Berg' was interpolated by someone who knew only the current office-holder's name, or the founding-era ice-memory has been overwritten by contemporary impressions so thoroughly that the chronicle's compiler could not distinguish them. I do not know which is worse. The entry required a source; this was the only one that names all three testers. I used it. I should not have used it without qualification, and the main text's clean prose makes me complicit in a falsehood I can identify but not yet correct.", type: :temporal, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771579366910_1", anchor: "This defacement appears to predate the shaping of the Berg itself", text: "Dated how? The ice holds no memory of the object. No mineral-layer analysis is cited because none exists — the Obelisk destroys the instruments. 'Appears to predate' is doing the work of a dating methodology that I do not have and neither does anyone else. I let this stand because every alternative phrasing was worse, but the reader deserves to know this is a guess dressed in passive voice.", type: :skepticism, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771579366910_2", anchor: "sealed by knowledge freely given rather than destroyed by force", text: "The mechanism maps exactly onto Way∴al doctrine — knowledge must flow freely; hoarded knowledge corrupts. Qeihong codified that framework decades after ☽'Saetacaeia-Viamana~ performed this act. Either Qeihong reverse-engineered theology from a successful containment protocol, or the doctrine predates her codification by longer than anyone has acknowledged. Given what I wrote in the Way∴al entry — that Qeihong built a tool, not a belief — the former explanation is damning. She studied what worked on this thing and sold it as philosophy.", type: :commentary, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771579366910_3", anchor: "The relevant strata contain a gap in the precise shape of a pillar", text: "I put personal testimony in the main text. I am aware this violates every standard I enforce on others. The gap is real. It is measurable. It has dimensions. And no one will ever corroborate it because my assistants were reassigned and the Foundation Depths are unvisited except by me and by whatever is carving channels downward through the strata above my archive. I recorded it in the entry because if this edition is the last — and commissioned retrospectives are never good news — then the gap goes into the record or it goes nowhere.", type: :commentary, display: :full, source_anchor: "the relevant strata contain a gap in the precise shape of a pillar"
  annotation "note_1771579366910_4", anchor: "A single pale tendril of new growth has since appeared at the base", text: "Coral does not grow on the Berg's surface. The water temperature required is available at exactly one location: the Corpse Current. The tendril is growing toward something, or the Corpse Current's reach is extending, or both. Cross-reference the Grandmother Deep entry on the current's expansion toward the Berg's foundations. The arithmetic is not complicated. I seem to keep writing that.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771579366910_5", anchor: "carved kill-counts: notches, tooth-marks, and sigils in no script recognized by any tradition of the Berg", text: "Not orca. Not penguin. Not the tunnel-chant marks I can barely read. The formations I will not describe from the pre-penguin strata of the Foundation Depths use similar non-repetitive patterning. Similar is not identical. I note the resemblance and leave it there because I am in a foul enough mood without speculating about what carved both.", type: :skepticism, display: :popout
